rived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["Mapped: OSM way431972186 v19 supplies actual rounded-square base corners, small annex and326m height/61levels. Ten original parts preserve tags/version/date and divide eight tapering shell sectors, the upper flat core and five-level annex. Main skin starts from the union of actual shell/core polygons; the taper finishes on mapped upper core1053143805, rather than a generic circular cylinder.","Resourced: individually inspected Commons Salesforce Tower2020(CC BY-SA4.0) shows continuous rounded corners, white horizontal sunshades and vertical fins; Salesforce Tower Roof(CC BY-SA4.0) shows the open mechanical crown and inset roof. CVU/CTBUH lists326.1m architecture,61above-ground floors and274.6m occupied height. OSM rounded326m is retained. No Salesforce Transit Center or neighboring tower is included.","Inferred: intermediate taper profiles, fin projection.18m, floor-band locations and crown screen spacing are authored from photographs, not new OSM tags. The four source corners and upper core are preserved; the8source roof:height245m bands are coarse taper descriptors rather than245m high literal shed roofs. Curtain-wall skins are opaque structural glass; supported window material occurs only on vertical stone lobby walls. The open crown, inset mechanical roof, mapped annex and326m top survive independently authored low LOD."],"source":{"url":"/objects/48efa02b14c22110b501db2cf766cf7a924fd459906ea1dfd359af923b7db495/source.blend.gz","bytes":328222,"sha256":"48efa02b14c22110b501db2cf766cf7a924fd459906ea1dfd359af923b7db495"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/fb1d62f798a102dd4bc742255dd86fad9a5a3c715b09782b74a5d322b62212e5/spatial-source.json","bytes":23990,"sha256":"fb1d62f798a